BT /F2 10 Tf 54 692 Td (PROBLEM) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 678 Td (Sort an array in nondecreasing order using divide and conquer.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 54 658 Td (DIVIDE) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 644 Td (Split the array into two halves until each subarray contains zero or one element.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 54 624 Td (CONQUER AND COMBINE) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 610 Td (Recursively sort both halves, then merge the two sorted halves by repeatedly taking the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 597 Td (    smaller front element.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 54 577 Td (PSEUDOCODE) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 563 Td (mergeSort\(A\):) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 550 Td (    if length\(A\) <= 1: return A) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 537 Td (    split A into L and R) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 524 Td (    return merge\(mergeSort\(L\), mergeSort\(R\)\)) Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 54 504 Td (EXAMPLE) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 490 Td ([7, 2, 6, 3] splits into [7,2] and [6,3], then merges to [2,3,6,7].) Tj ET
